.TH CORRESYNC 1 "July 2026" "Corresync" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
corresync \- local-first Outlook Web mail and calendar CLI and MCP server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B corresync
.RI [ --config " path" ]
.RI [ --version ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B corresync
controls an explicitly authorized Outlook Web session through a dedicated,
interactive browser profile. It does not require a Microsoft Graph application,
accept a password, persist browser authorization material, or intercept TLS.
.PP
CLI and MCP calls use the same typed application operations, deterministic
policy checks, content-free audit boundary, and authenticated local session
owner. Consequential external writes require an exact preview followed by a
separate commit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B config
Create, locate, show, read, update, edit, and strictly validate the secret-free
configuration.
.TP
.B doctor
Diagnose local prerequisites and optionally probe Outlook Web compatibility.
.TP
.B auth
Open interactive Outlook Web sign-in, inspect content-free session state, or
close browsers and clear every in-memory session.
.TP
.B mail
Discover folders; list, search, and read messages; create drafts; send reviewed
new messages, replies, and forwards; retrieve bounded attachments; move,
hard-delete, and set read state.
.TP
.B calendar
List calendar event metadata in a bounded time window, or review and create one
typed event with optional all-day, reminder, recurrence, attendee, and Teams
link settings. Versioned update and cancellation commands use exact previews
and commits without enabling general Teams access.
.TP
.B daemon
Start, inspect, or stop the authenticated local session owner.
.TP
.B mcp
Run the local stdio MCP server, register it through supported client CLIs, or
print native client configuration.
.TP
.B update
Check the latest stable public release. Explicitly self-update a direct
installation after signed provenance and platform verification, or print the
owner-specific command for a package-managed installation.
.TP
.B completion
Generate a Bash, Zsh, or Fish completion script, or detect and idempotently
install completion for the current shell.
.TP
.B version
Print build and version information.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
corresync --version
corresync help auth
corresync config init
corresync config set accounts.work.origin https://outlook.cloud.microsoft
corresync auth login
corresync auth status
corresync mail list --limit 25
corresync calendar list --start 2026-07-17T00:00:00Z \
  --end 2026-07-18T00:00:00Z
corresync calendar create --subject "Design review" \
  --start 2026-07-20T09:00:00Z --end 2026-07-20T10:00:00Z \
  --teams-meeting
# Review the output, then repeat with --approve.
corresync calendar update --event-id EVENT --change-key KEY \
  --subject "Updated design review"
corresync calendar cancel --event-id EVENT --change-key KEY
# Both commands preview only; repeat with --approve to commit.
corresync mcp setup codex
corresync mcp setup claude-code
corresync mcp setup github-copilot
corresync mcp setup gemini-cli
corresync mcp setup qwen-code
corresync mcp setup qoder
corresync completion install
corresync update
corresync update check
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
An operation or diagnostic failed.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was invalid.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable terminal color and styling when set to any value.
.TP
.B TERM=dumb
Disable terminal color and styling.
.TP
.B VISUAL
Editor command used by
.BR "corresync config edit" .
.TP
.B EDITOR
Fallback editor command used when
.B VISUAL
is unset.
.SH SECURITY
Mail and calendar content is untrusted private input. Review exact previews
before committing a write. Approval tokens are short-lived secret capabilities
and must not be logged or persisted. If a write reports an unknown outcome,
inspect mailbox state before retrying.
.PP
Only use
.B corresync
with accounts and data you are authorized to access. Undocumented Outlook Web contracts
can change without notice; run
.B corresync doctor --online
after an update or unexplained compatibility failure.
.PP
Automatic update checks read only public release metadata, cache results for
24 hours, and never write notices to MCP, completion, daemon, piped, or JSON
output. Only an explicit
.B corresync update
may replace a verified direct installation; package-manager files are never
modified. Set CORRESYNC_NO_UPDATE_CHECK=1 or configure disable_automatic_checks to
opt out of startup checks.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I config.toml
The effective path is printed by
.BR "corresync config path" .
It contains account aliases, Outlook Web origins, browser settings, and policy only; it
must not contain passwords, cookies, bearer tokens, or canary values.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR corresync (1)
command-specific help is available from
.BR "corresync command --help"
or
.BR "corresync help command" .
Project documentation and the security policy are distributed with release
archives and native packages.
